+
+/// locateSymbolAt for an #include line (as the AST path, anywhere on the line),
+/// answered from the include graph of the file's shard: the file's direct
+/// include whose path ends with the spelled name. Answers only when \p Content
+/// is the text the shard was built from (errors elsewhere in the file do not
+/// matter) and exactly one direct include matches; std::nullopt otherwise
+/// (also for "." / ".." components and macro includes). Callers then use the
+/// AST.
+std::optional<LocatedSymbol> locateIncludeFromShard(const IndexFileIn &Shard,
+                                                    llvm::StringRef MainFilePath,
+                                                    llvm::StringRef Content,
+                                                    Position Pos);
+
 /// Returns the symbols referenced at \p Pos of the file \p MainFilePath, looked
